Subject: uhttpd: update to 2026-11-05

The web server from OpenWrt main as of 5 November 2026 instead of the one
of 3 August. Upstream fixes since then:

- request parsing stays inside the bytes that were received
  (GHSA-788h-w5m4-j5xv);
- a script slot is released when the peer closes with an unfinished body,
  and one address can hold only part of the slots, half of max_requests
  unless max_requests_per_source says otherwise (GHSA-p2hf-3hpj-hfpc);
- Basic Auth realms are enforced for URL-prefix handlers
  (GHSA-5cgm-8h9x-v28c);
- ubus list requests with non-string parameters are refused, and the list
  answer stays within what can be encoded;
- TCP_NODELAY on accepted sockets;
- the ID in a generated certificate no longer loses repeated bytes;
- an instance can run in a VRF.

OpenWrt commits c6c02f7e79, 26410f4160, 076b3e767b, 20c44f41b2 and
955b582a66, taken as they are.

